    "created_at": "2017-02-15T17:14:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-15T17:14:17Z",
    "body": "> the question is whether the CSS concept of \"display: contents should behave a certain way\" should map exactly to the HTML concept of \"has a form owner\"\r\n\r\nI don't think it maps exactly.  An `<object>` showing fallback content should have `display:contents` work on it, for example.  Same thing for `<img>` showing its alt text.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
