    "body": "Updated Display to refer to “form controls” with “(such as submittable elements in HTML)” for now... ping me or Tab to update if there ends up being a better target.\r\n\r\nI'd prefer if legend, meter, progress, and details didn't have to go in the \"special cases where we hide all the content\" case.\r\n\r\nWe're making a special case because replaced elements and form controls are categories where the behavior of \"remove the element's own frame but leave its contents\" is essentially undefined; and we're additionally trying to make the set of elements so affected an understandable set to the author. (E.g. we're including `<button>` even though we could probably just strip it of its buttonness and render its contents because most other form controls are going to disappear, including buttons created with `<input>`.) I'm otherwise in favor of minimizing the set to the extent that we can.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
